  "claim": "Travis Oates voiced the character that translates to the Finnish 'Sisu Nasu' in the 2011 movie. The Jungle Book was released before this movie.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Winnie the Pooh (2011 film). Sentence: Winnie the Pooh is a 2011 American animated buddy musical comedy film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: The Jungle Book (1994 film). Sentence: Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book is a 1994 live-action American adventure film co-written and directed by Stephen Sommers, produced by Edward S. Feldman and Raju Patel, from a story by Ronald Yanover and Mark Geldman.\nPage: Travis Oates. Sentence: He and Jim Cummings were the only two original voice actors to return for the 2011 movie.\nPage: Sisu Nasu. Sentence: The Nasu (acronym for \"Nauha-Sisu\" English: Track Sisu , also meaning \"Piglet\" in Finnish) is a tracked articulated, all-terrain transport vehicle developed by Sisu Auto for the Finnish Army.",
