        "original_id": "4e91871f-1c93-5cd6-99b0-a091afb4ccd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Winnie the Pooh (2011 film), Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book, Nasu\n- Companies: Walt Disney Animation Studios, Walt Disney Pictures, Sisu Auto\n- People: Stephen Sommers, Edward S. Feldman, Raju Patel, Ronald Yanover, Mark Geldman, Travis Oates, Jim Cummings\n- Organizations: Finnish Army\n\nFacts:\n- Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book is a 1994 live-action American adventure film.\n- Stephen Sommers co-wrote and directed Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book.\n- Edward S. Feldman and Raju Patel produced Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book from a story by Ronald Yanover and Mark Geldman.\n- Winnie the Pooh is a 2011 American animated buddy musical comedy film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- Travis Oates and Jim Cummings were the only two original voice actors to return for the 2011 Winnie the Pooh movie.\n- The Nasu is a tracked articulated all-terrain transport vehicle developed by Sisu Auto for the Finnish Army.\n- The name Nasu is an acronym for \"Nauha-Sisu,\" meaning \"Track Sisu,\" and it also means \"Piglet\" in Finnish.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
